  "key": "country",
  "rule": "language of government publication (de facto), with English always included. A language enters a country's row if government institutions at the tiers the frame samples publish primary web content in it. Established by direct observation for 28 countries -- 12 on a pre-committed 12-site sample, 16 on a 4-site verification -- at >=25% of reachable sites at any frame-sampled tier; the remaining 197 countries are graded expert guesses, unverified. English is included for every country by policy, independent of observation. A row is revisited when its country's Stage 2 yield falls materially below its stratum peers, or when a named open question in SIGNATURE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md has its blocker clear. Protocol v1 PI-ruled 2026-08-29; rows PI-signed 2026-08-30.",
  "always_include": [
    "en"
  ],
  "subnational_note": "One answer per country, applied to every institution in it. That is crudest exactly where the frame is densest: an Indian block does not publish in the same language as another state's block, and the signed table has no subnational grain to say so. Caveats C1-C7 in SIGNATURE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md name the draws that would settle the known cases.",
